---
title: Thai Sweet Chilli Sauce
course: Condiment
locale: en_GB
prep time: 15m
cook time: 5m
difficulty: Easy
cuisine: Thai
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- thai
- savoury
- condiment
- vegetarian
---

In a blender purée together the @garlic cloves{3%large}(peeled), @red jalapeño or serrano peppers{2}(optionally deseeded), @vinegar{4%tbsp}, @sugar{100%g}, @water{170%ml}, and @salt{0.5%tbsp}.

Transfer the mixture to a #saucepan and bring to a boil over a medium-high heat. Lower the heat to medium and simmer until the mixture thickens a bit and the garlic begins to soften, about ~{3%minutes}.

Combine the @cornflour{1%tbsp} and @water{2%tbsp} to make a paste. Whisk in the cornflour and continue to simmer for a further ~{1%minute}.

Let cool completely before storing in a glass jar and refrigerating.